<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Madame Curie is seen in hematology one week after her primary care visit, where two months of fatigue, breathlessness on stairs, easy bruising, and a recent fever led to a blood count showing pancytopenia with a low reticulocyte count. She received two units of irradiated red cells that day. She is less breathless since the transfusion but still tires by midafternoon. New bruises appear on her arms and shins without injury; she has had no nosebleeds, gum bleeding, blood in the urine or stool, or further fever. She has worked for decades with radium sources and X-ray equipment, much of it before modern shielding, and she has stopped laboratory work since the last visit. She wants the data and the plan in detail. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Since the transfusion</td><td>Less breathless; fatigue by midafternoon</td></tr><tr><td>Bleeding</td><td>Bruises on arms and shins without injury; no mucosal, urinary, or bowel bleeding</td></tr><tr><td>Infection</td><td>No fever since the first visit</td></tr><tr><td>Exposure</td><td>Decades of occupational ionizing radiation; no further exposure since the first visit</td></tr><tr><td>Patient preference</td><td>Wants the full data and plan</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.18"/>
    <code code="10187-3" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Review of systems Narrative - Reported"/>
    <title>Review of Systems</title>
    <text><table><thead><tr><th>System</th><th>Result</th><th>Finding</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Constitutional</td><td>Positive</td><td>Fatigue by midafternoon; no fever, night sweats, or weight loss</td></tr><tr><td>Hematologic</td><td>Positive</td><td>Easy bruising; no mucosal bleeding</td></tr><tr><td>Cardiovascular</td><td>Positive</td><td>Breathless on stairs, better since transfusion; no chest pain</td></tr><tr><td>Eyes</td><td>Positive</td><td>Glare and blurred reading vision in the right eye</td></tr><tr><td>Skin</td><td>Positive</td><td>Thin, scarred fingertips; no rash</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>5 systems reviewed. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
</component>

